menu "Network link (WiFi station)"

config NETLINK_SSID0
    string "Seed WiFi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        First entry of the NVS credential table, written on first boot if
        the table is empty. Leave blank in committed defaults.

config NETLINK_PASS0
    string "Seed WiFi password"
    default ""


config NETLINK_MAX_CREDS
    int "Credential table size"
    default 8
    range 1 16
    help
        How many SSID/password pairs NVS holds. Eight covers a home
        network, a bench network and a few moves.

config NETLINK_ROAM_RSSI
    int "Roam-check threshold (dBm)"
    default -70
    range -95 -40
    help
        Below this the driver raises WIFI_EVENT_STA_BSS_RSSI_LOW and the
        station scans for a better AP on the same SSID. Inherited from
        relo-bridge, where beacon timeouts began around -75 dBm.

config NETLINK_MAX_BACKOFF_MS
    int "Reconnect backoff ceiling (ms)"
    default 30000
    range 1000 300000

config NETLINK_JOIN_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Time allowed from associate to IP (ms)"
    default 15000
    range 3000 60000
    help
        An association that never yields an address (wrong VLAN, DHCP
        exhausted) is a failure for that credential this cycle, so the
        station moves to the next one instead of sitting on a dead link.

endmenu
